 how to defeat the dead but once again  this fell on deaf ears  so instead Sam put his own plan into  action  once again Sam Gilly and the baby left  in the middle of the night but before  they left Sam had to steal something  again just like he did before he left  his house  Sam went into the library and took all  kinds of books and documents so that  could potentially give him answers about  the night King when Sam packed up their  carriage to leave you could see that he  still had hearts bein with him wrapped  up in the same blanket he had before so  the sword is in Winterfell with Sam and  Gilly I highly doubt that they had been  having Sam carry around this sword just  for shits and giggles the North will be  ground zero for the Great War and it's  no coincidence that all of the magical  swords will be in the North at the same  time heart's pain will be put to good  use in some way the Valyrian steel  dagger popped back up in the North right  before the battle was going to kick off  and Jaime Lannister is bringing the  other half of ice so we should see all  of these weapons play their part when  they need them the most one thing I am  wondering is what could possibly be in  all of those books and documents Sam  took from the Citadel is it possible  that Sam finds something on one of those  pages that gives him an idea of what to  do with hearts Bane I know we've all  been wondering if someone will ever  discover the methods to making Valyrian  steel could Sam possibly have that  information with him and he doesn't even  know it yet you also have to consider  what type of sword hearts Bane is hearts  Bane is a two-handed great sword which  means it's very big given the size of  hearts Bane it could easily be melted  down and made into more than one weapon  all you would need is someone that knew  how to reforge it and if they were going  to have anyone do this Gendry would  probably be the man for the job  Gendry disappeared from multiple seasons  but since they brought him back you have  to assume he will have a role to play in  the endgame this is interesting because  Sam and Hearts Bane are now in  Winterfell in Gendry is on his way there  - and he also have to keep in mind the  only reason why Davos went looking for  Gendry in the first place was because he  knew John was going to need blacksmiths  to turn all the dragon glass into  weapons Davos told ginjury he was  sending him to Winterfell to work in  their forges but as we all know  Gendry just couldn't keep his mouth shut  Gentry did end up revealing his identity  to John and he ended up going along with  them on their mission beyond the wall  but now that their mission  / gang jury will resume his role as one  of the blacksmiths in Winterfell now I  know what some of you may be thinking  now that John has all of this dragon  class do they even need hearts pain  since dragonglass kills White Walkers -  that is a very valid point because you  don't need as much Valyrian steel when  you have a mountain of dragonglass  but you have to think of it like this  why would they have Sam steel this sword  and not put it to good use it would  completely defeat the purpose of Sam  taking it he obviously took it because  he knew it would be needed but on the  other hand I don't actually think Sam is  gonna be the one to use the sword  himself now I know Sam was able to kill  a white Walker back in season 2 but  let's be honest he kind of got lucky  it's not like he went toe-to-toe with  the white Walker he actually just  stabbed him in the back fighting a white  Walker face-to-face is a completely  different story and I doubt it's  something Sam wants to do I personally  think Sam will let someone else carry  hearts Bane or he will turn it into  several weapons if that's even possible  I can't guarantee if Gendry has the  ability to do this or not but I don't  think it's out of the realm of  possibility demand again sure he worked  for was named table Beaumont and in the  bulks he knew how to rework Valyrian  steel he was actually the same person  who turns the ice into two swords and  since Gendry worked with him for several  years there is a slight chance that  ginjury may have learned this skill from  him but they could just be waiting to  reveal this information in the final  season I don't think there are any  coincidences in this story only a  handful of people know how to reforge  Valyrian steel and Gendry just happened  to work for one of the men that did  George probably added that little layer  that way he could use it later on in the  story but this is just my opinion I know  most people don't agree with that  however I only give it a fifty-fifty  chance to happen in this show but in the  books I feel pretty confident it's going  to happen eventually even though I don't  think Sam will carry the sword himself I  will admit that there is a chance that  he could maybe he does it out of spite  or out of pride because his father told  him he never would Jon Snow has one hell  of a Suicide Squad ready to fight beside  him but the only problem is Jon is the  only one that had  of Valyrian steel weapon John has all of  these great sword fighters in the north  but they aren't properly equipped  I mean sure they could use a dragon  glass dagger but a swordsman needs a  sword in Hearts Bane is the perfect  weapon to carry into battle against the  army of the dead and you're not just  going to have some random solider using  hearts bane  a sword like this needs to be in the  hands of one of the main characters  John has Valyrian steel Arya has  Valyrian steel jamie has Valyrian steel  and Brienne has Valyrian steel  beric Dondarrion already has a flaming  sword so that leaves only a few top  fighters that could be worthy of using  hearts pain you have tormund Giantsbane  Jorah Mormont and the Hound these three  men would be my three picks if anyone  was going to use the sword since Hart's  Bane is a two-handed great sword The  Hound would probably be able to carry it  and swing it the easiest since he is so  big and strong but Sam has had no  interactions with him at all he might  not be willing to just hand it over to a  stranger but that doesn't mean the Hound  won't get it because when Sam sees him  he might just hand it over  also the Hound did say he always wanted  some Valyrian steel so perhaps he  finally gets his wish but I don't think  it's as likely as one of these other  candidates  tormund could easily do some damage with  it and he doesn't know Sam from their  time spent together at Castle black  but tormund doesn't typically carry a  sword he uses a different type of blade  although I am sure he would love to use  some Valyrian steel I mean who wouldn't  want to in my opinion I think Jorah  Mormont has the best chance of using  hearts bane Sam immediately had some  respect for Jorah simply because of who  his father was this was one of the  reasons why Sam wanted to help save  Dora's life in the first place and this  is when these two started to build a  friendly relationship with one another  he father saved me more than once it's  the least I could do oops a possible  cross again  I hope they do  not only did Sam and Jorah become  friends but Jorah is also a very  competent swordsman although he has  passed as prime John Snow now carries  house Mormons ancestral Valyrian steel  sword John did try to give it back to  Jorah but he did not want it but perhaps  Jorah could still end up using a  Valyrian steel sword if Sam would allow  him to carry it into battle  I think Hart's Bane would be deadlier if  it were in the hands of the Hound but I  could see Sam letting Jorah use it  before he would let the Hound use it but  I could be wrong about that there is one  other thing I want to mention about  hearts Bane before I end the video the  name of this sword itself could indicate  that it has a big role to play in the  end it might be too obvious for it to be  true but since it's called 